WEBVTT

00:00.830 --> 00:04.010
Yaga, what is that thing?

00:04.480 --> 00:06.760
It is possible to have
man-made cursed corpses

00:06.760 --> 00:10.840
act more autonomously than
other forms of manipulation.

00:10.840 --> 00:13.080
But they're always powered by

00:13.080 --> 00:15.860
consuming cursed energy
from the sorcerer.

00:15.860 --> 00:20.370
Yet that thing is sustaining
itself on its own cursed energy.

00:22.230 --> 00:25.570
The higher-ups are currently trying
to designate you as a special-grade

00:25.570 --> 00:28.960
and officially sentence you
to indefinite imprisonment.

00:29.780 --> 00:33.810
Because if you can intentionally
create that thing,

00:33.810 --> 00:37.310
you could easily have your own army.

00:38.010 --> 00:40.260
Answer me, Yaga.

00:41.430 --> 00:47.020
Do you truly not know how
that thing was made?

00:49.750 --> 00:50.630
Correct.

00:51.820 --> 00:53.370
Masamichi.

00:54.410 --> 00:56.380
Everyone's worried about you.

00:56.380 --> 00:57.950
They say you seem down.

00:58.200 --> 00:59.630
I see.

01:01.950 --> 01:03.920
So I told them all this!

01:03.920 --> 01:06.910
If you're feeling down,
we just have to cheer you up!

01:09.300 --> 01:10.570
That so?

01:11.250 --> 01:12.730
I'm a genius, aren't I?

01:13.250 --> 01:14.700
Yeah.

01:15.670 --> 01:19.550
Takeru, I'm sorry, but I won't be
able to come home for a while.

01:19.960 --> 01:22.270
Please let the others know, too.

01:22.270 --> 01:24.080
Leaving for work again?

01:24.080 --> 01:26.960
Yeah. It'll be a long trip.

01:26.960 --> 01:28.190
Don't worry.

01:28.190 --> 01:31.540
This forest is protected by Tengen-sama.

01:31.540 --> 01:35.200
Your mother will come see you again, too.

01:36.620 --> 01:39.690
You'll be all right without me.

01:43.090 --> 01:44.490
Masamichi.

01:45.160 --> 01:47.870
It'll be lonely without you, Masamichi.

01:52.910 --> 01:55.250
Are you sure, Kusakabe?

01:55.250 --> 01:58.380
Don't go telling anyone I helped you.

01:58.380 --> 02:01.760
You were captured to lure Yaga-san out.

02:02.760 --> 02:05.510
And I owe that man a favor.

02:06.550 --> 02:08.370
Go on, get!

02:09.810 --> 02:11.730
You're really sure about this?

02:12.300 --> 02:14.690
This thing is not your nephew.

02:14.690 --> 02:17.110
It's just something with
your nephew's information.

02:17.440 --> 02:19.890
You're trying to tell me
I can't live in the present

02:19.890 --> 02:23.260
if I stay hung up on the
dead forever, right?

02:24.560 --> 02:25.940
Still...

02:25.940 --> 02:31.240
My little sister can no longer
live without Takeru.

02:35.530 --> 02:39.580
Masamichi, that lady's
my mother, isn't she?

02:40.280 --> 02:43.470
Yeah. Good job recognizing her.

02:45.470 --> 02:47.350
I had a feeling it was her.

02:50.160 --> 02:51.640
I'm a genius, aren't I?

02:58.070 --> 02:59.190
Takeru!

03:03.340 --> 03:06.000
Takeru!

03:10.290 --> 03:11.650
I'm sorry, but...

03:12.250 --> 03:13.840
I know.

03:13.840 --> 03:17.700
You can't let the existence of your fully
autonomous cursed corpses become known.

03:18.320 --> 03:20.050
So he can't live with her.

03:20.050 --> 03:21.520
I'm sorry.

03:21.520 --> 03:23.670
Why are you apologizing?

03:24.950 --> 03:26.730
Thanks a lot.

03:27.770 --> 03:28.920
I mean it.

03:29.880 --> 03:30.970
Thank you.

03:32.690 --> 03:37.110
Where do you think you're going without
any cursed corpses, Principal Yaga?

03:38.110 --> 03:39.900
To see my son.

03:40.220 --> 03:41.940
Since you've been sentenced to death,

03:41.940 --> 03:44.980
allow me to tell you the
one way to save your life.

03:45.390 --> 03:50.370
Disclose how you create those fully
autonomous man-made cursed corpses!

03:51.420 --> 03:55.120
You all sure grew bold the
moment Satoru was gone.

04:25.690 --> 04:26.610
Principal.

04:27.230 --> 04:30.560
I'll handle the rest, so you may leave.

04:30.560 --> 04:31.530
Understood.

04:32.850 --> 04:38.310
You use the body's information to
reproduce the soul's information.

04:38.310 --> 04:42.710
Then you place that soul information
in the cursed corpse's core.

04:45.890 --> 04:48.240
That's not enough, though.

04:48.240 --> 04:51.100
You have to place cores housing
three highly compatible souls

04:51.100 --> 04:53.060
into a single cursed corpse,

04:53.730 --> 04:57.850
and make those souls observe
each other at all times.

04:58.230 --> 04:59.990
Doing that

04:59.990 --> 05:04.200
finally allows the souls to stabilize
so self-awareness can take root.

05:04.200 --> 05:06.830
Roughly three months after that's born,

05:06.830 --> 05:09.520
it will begin supplying
its own cursed energy.

05:09.520 --> 05:10.970
Why?!

05:12.510 --> 05:14.670
Why share that now?!

05:15.660 --> 05:18.250
Why wouldn't you reveal that sooner?!

05:18.250 --> 05:20.740
Why didn't you try to live longer?!

05:21.450 --> 05:23.210
Because...

05:23.210 --> 05:26.490
it's a curse, Principal Gakuganji.

05:27.000 --> 05:31.240
A curse from me to you.

05:34.950 --> 05:36.110
Masamichi!

05:46.540 --> 05:48.610
Why don't you fight?

05:48.610 --> 05:50.530
Do you not hate me?

05:51.410 --> 05:54.050
Pandas aren't bound by things like that.

05:54.800 --> 05:58.150
Besides, you were never on
bad terms with Masamichi.

05:59.000 --> 06:03.050
To me, you're just the
knife that fell upon him.

06:04.760 --> 06:08.050
Just make sure you remember this...

06:08.470 --> 06:12.050
Even pandas cry.

06:30.450 --> 06:31.160
JUJUTSU KAISEN

06:54.430 --> 06:58.640
JUJUTSU KAISEN
The Culling Game Part 1

07:50.390 --> 07:54.380
Kinji Hakari is currently earning money
as a bookie for a fight club he's running

07:54.380 --> 07:57.490
in an abandoned multi-story
parking garage in Tochigi Prefecture.

07:57.950 --> 07:59.440
A fight club?

07:59.440 --> 08:02.000
They host fist fights between sorcerers.

08:02.000 --> 08:03.930
Then the spectators are...

08:03.930 --> 08:06.250
Generally non-sorcerers.

08:06.760 --> 08:11.190
That blatantly violates the secrecy
mandated in Article 8 of the Jujutsu Code.

08:09.000 --> 08:10.590
ARTICLE 8 - SECRECY: SORCERERS MUST NOT
REVEAL THE EXISTENCE OF SORCERY, CURSES,
AND CURSED OBJECTS TO NON-SORCERERS.
HOWEVER, THIS SHALL NOT APPLY WHEN
IT IS NECESSARY TO FULFILL
THE DUTIES OF THE PREVIOUS ARTICLE.

08:10.590 --> 08:12.970
SECRECY

08:11.730 --> 08:15.140
There are probably curse users among
the participants in the fights, as well.

08:15.140 --> 08:17.040
Do be careful.

08:20.050 --> 08:21.270
Why are we changing?

08:21.610 --> 08:24.750
Hakari-san was expelled for
clashing with the upper brass.

08:24.750 --> 08:27.240
He's also actively violating
jujutsu regulations.

08:27.650 --> 08:30.890
If he finds out we're with
Jujutsu High, he might run.

08:30.890 --> 08:33.160
It's like we're cops and he's the robber.

08:33.810 --> 08:34.900
Hmm?

08:35.200 --> 08:37.370
We're on Jujutsu High's side now?

08:37.370 --> 08:38.890
We're in a gray zone,

08:38.890 --> 08:41.690
but in Hakari-san's eyes,
at least, we're with them.

08:41.690 --> 08:44.170
Is he likely to cooperate
with us in the first place?

08:44.170 --> 08:45.670
I'm not sure.

08:45.670 --> 08:48.350
All our senpai say he's
a good-for-nothing,

08:49.030 --> 08:52.430
but Okkotsu-senpai claimed
he's stronger than him.

08:53.340 --> 08:55.060
We definitely want his strength.

08:55.650 --> 08:57.170
Go home, brats.

08:57.530 --> 08:59.810
This isn't a place for you to hang out.

08:59.810 --> 09:02.470
You have until the count
of three to turn around.

09:02.470 --> 09:05.270
Any other choices will
earn a beating from me.

09:05.270 --> 09:06.640
We need money.

09:06.640 --> 09:09.150
Let us enter the fights held here.

09:11.880 --> 09:13.570
The first rule is:

09:14.000 --> 09:16.830
You do not talk about the fight club.

09:17.420 --> 09:19.720
Now answer me. Who told you?

09:19.720 --> 09:22.040
You'll get your beating after that.

09:22.040 --> 09:23.550
I don't know his name.

09:23.550 --> 09:24.580
I killed him.

09:25.290 --> 09:26.850
It was about a month ago.

09:27.260 --> 09:29.620
He was some scumbag who was all talk.

09:29.620 --> 09:32.370
Kondo disappeared about a month ago.

09:33.210 --> 09:35.140
I'll fill his slot for you.

09:35.550 --> 09:39.110
Or would you rather I lay you
out in front of the bookie?

09:39.110 --> 09:42.900
Oh, yeah. He'd be wary if we
suddenly asked to see him.

09:42.900 --> 09:45.410
I guess we shouldn't know
his name's Hakari, either.

09:42.900 --> 09:43.670
Yes.

09:44.400 --> 09:46.400
No, there's no proof.

09:45.730 --> 09:47.210
Time to zip the lips.

09:46.860 --> 09:47.900
Are you sure?

09:48.570 --> 09:49.970
That's enough.

09:50.660 --> 09:52.650
The boss has given you the go-ahead.

09:52.650 --> 09:55.460
We'll pit you against
today's seeded fighter.

09:55.460 --> 09:56.780
However...

09:56.780 --> 09:58.620
he's the one fighting.

10:00.800 --> 10:02.120
That's good for us.

10:02.120 --> 10:04.360
Itadori's better suited to the fighting.

10:04.760 --> 10:06.830
No go. I'll fight.

10:06.830 --> 10:09.160
Boss said he doesn't like you.

10:07.160 --> 10:09.170
Boss

10:09.590 --> 10:11.740
If you don't like it, the deal's off.

10:12.940 --> 10:15.470
Fine. We'll take it, then.

10:15.940 --> 10:17.920
Fushiguro, that was risky.

10:17.920 --> 10:19.470
Your bluffs went too far.

10:19.470 --> 10:20.920
That's not actually true.

10:21.380 --> 10:25.510
If curse users are participating too,
that means there must be decent turnover.

10:25.930 --> 10:26.930
More importantly...

10:26.930 --> 10:28.750
Yeah, they're here.

10:29.180 --> 10:31.820
If he was watching us
through security cameras,

10:32.130 --> 10:35.110
there's a high chance
Hakari-senpai is in here.

10:35.110 --> 10:37.840
Itadori, you snoop around
from the inside.

10:37.840 --> 10:41.130
I'll snoop around that parking
lot in the meantime.

10:41.130 --> 10:41.810
Maybe.

10:41.810 --> 10:42.880
Maybe?

10:42.880 --> 10:44.860
He's probably leaving me
to my own devices.

10:44.860 --> 10:46.690
If he learns we're infiltrating his club,

10:46.690 --> 10:50.210
we'll lose his trust and our opportunity
to make contact with Hakari-san.

10:50.570 --> 10:53.670
Well, we'll just resort to
force if that happens.

10:53.960 --> 10:56.250
That's really our last resort.

10:56.250 --> 11:01.010
We're only here to ask Hakari-san
for his cooperation.

11:01.010 --> 11:03.890
I'd like to avoid anything that'll
affect our future relations.

11:04.500 --> 11:07.460
To be honest, I don't think I
should be doing anything tonight.

11:08.040 --> 11:10.810
But I don't want to waste the time
we have until Tsumiki is required

11:10.810 --> 11:12.710
to declare her participation
in the Culling Game.

11:13.430 --> 11:14.860
Right now...

11:14.860 --> 11:16.590
it's 5 PM on the 10th.

11:17.080 --> 11:18.990
So nine days until the deadline, huh?

11:18.990 --> 11:22.410
It took longer to get
here than we thought.

11:22.770 --> 11:26.170
That's why I'll be trying to
look for Hakari-san tonight,

11:26.650 --> 11:28.940
but if it looks risky, I'll pull out.

11:28.940 --> 11:30.630
That's why I say "maybe."

11:30.630 --> 11:31.550
Got it.

11:33.540 --> 11:35.390
There are only two rules.

11:35.390 --> 11:38.050
No running away,
and no using cursed techniques.

11:38.050 --> 11:38.980
How come?

11:38.980 --> 11:42.030
I don't mind if they're
using cursed techniques.

11:42.030 --> 11:44.100
Because most of the spectators
are non-sorcerers,

11:44.100 --> 11:45.490
those who can't see them.

11:45.490 --> 11:48.000
A fight people can't see
won't excite them.

11:48.350 --> 11:49.970
And the "no running" rule?

11:50.250 --> 11:53.480
It means you fight where
the spectators can see you.

11:53.480 --> 11:55.850
It's all about the spectators, huh?

11:55.850 --> 11:57.140
Of course.

11:57.140 --> 11:58.350
This is a business.

11:58.960 --> 12:00.430
What's the boss like?

12:01.790 --> 12:02.810
You curious?

12:03.460 --> 12:04.770
Well, yeah.

12:05.340 --> 12:06.910
You'll know if you meet him.

12:06.910 --> 12:07.920
Can I meet him?

12:09.210 --> 12:11.280
There are two kinds of matches.

12:11.280 --> 12:15.170
Real beat-downs, like in today's
tournament, and fixed bouts.

12:15.660 --> 12:17.780
The boss writes the script for those.

12:18.340 --> 12:21.300
He might call for you if you
manage to shine out there.

12:21.960 --> 12:24.920
In other words, I just need
to put on a good show.

12:24.920 --> 12:27.250
That makes things simple.

12:36.810 --> 12:39.970
That's your opponent.

12:42.590 --> 12:45.960
I was blown away the first
time I saw him, too.

12:45.960 --> 12:46.610
Yeah.

12:47.230 --> 12:49.540
It's really all about
drawing in the crowd.

12:51.900 --> 12:54.500
Now, we're getting started again tonight!

12:54.500 --> 12:57.530
It's time for the
Gachinko Fight Club Tournament!

12:57.530 --> 13:01.110
Commentary will be provided by me,
your very own John☆Bobby!

13:01.110 --> 13:04.490
Allow me to introduce tonight's
exciting match-up!

13:04.490 --> 13:06.330
We're joined by a sudden upstart!

13:06.330 --> 13:08.240
Will he rise up or burn out?!

13:08.240 --> 13:13.170
It's the Dangerous Fireball Kid,
Yuji Itadori!

13:13.170 --> 13:18.690
He stands like a panda, sits like
a panda, and walks like a panda!

13:18.690 --> 13:22.630
It's Panda!

13:21.820 --> 13:24.990
Fighting Arena

13:21.820 --> 13:24.990
2nd Floor CH 6

13:22.630 --> 13:24.270
Now, place your bets, place your bets!

13:24.270 --> 13:25.470
Everyone ready?!

13:25.470 --> 13:27.610
Let's get ready to rumble!

13:27.610 --> 13:30.530
I can feel my passion draining away.

13:30.530 --> 13:32.700
What's wrong, Kin-chan?

13:32.700 --> 13:36.560
Luck is meant to be tested, you know.

13:36.560 --> 13:38.920
It's boring to gamble when you
know who'll win from the start.

13:39.370 --> 13:43.580
There aren't many stray sorcerers
who are tough enough to beat Panda.

13:43.580 --> 13:44.930
Whoa!

13:44.930 --> 13:48.680
This is the best bout in my
career as a commentator!

13:45.320 --> 13:47.300
Looks like you might be wrong.

13:47.300 --> 13:48.410
Huh?

13:48.680 --> 13:50.980
Fighting Arena

13:48.680 --> 13:50.980
2nd Floor CH 6

13:52.990 --> 13:55.460
Have you been able to see Hakari-senpai?

13:55.870 --> 13:56.670
No.

13:57.810 --> 13:58.520
Tap

14:01.830 --> 14:04.470
He's not wary of me since
we know each other,

14:04.470 --> 14:06.020
but he's avoiding me.

14:06.200 --> 14:07.280
Tap Tap Tap Tap

14:07.860 --> 14:09.110
Roooar

14:09.110 --> 14:10.450
Roooar

14:10.710 --> 14:14.280
The other third-year's
technique is also a problem.

14:23.510 --> 14:26.250
You're hiding the fact that you're
from Jujutsu High, right?

14:26.250 --> 14:27.330
Yeah.

14:28.750 --> 14:29.990
Good, good.

14:29.990 --> 14:31.470
You know what to do now, right?

14:37.640 --> 14:38.680
Whoa!

14:38.680 --> 14:42.880
This is definitely the best bout
in my career as a commentator!

14:42.880 --> 14:45.980
Though I've only been one for two weeks!

14:50.860 --> 14:51.610
Tap

14:53.410 --> 14:53.710
Tap

14:55.700 --> 14:56.240
Tap

14:57.330 --> 15:00.000
Tap Tap Tap

15:04.380 --> 15:04.880
Tap

15:11.260 --> 15:14.850
The winner: Itadori!

15:15.480 --> 15:17.750
What a punch!

15:17.750 --> 15:18.810
I can't move!

15:18.810 --> 15:22.970
The SPCA won't stand for this!

15:23.220 --> 15:24.600
Your acting sucks.

15:23.440 --> 15:24.600
Your acting sucks.

15:24.600 --> 15:28.260
Send Itadori up to the roof
when the tournament's over.

15:28.260 --> 15:28.890
Huh?

15:28.890 --> 15:30.380
He's sure to win it.

15:30.380 --> 15:33.540
Plus, he's intentionally
fighting in three dimensions

15:33.540 --> 15:35.760
to wow the spectators on the upper floors.

15:35.760 --> 15:37.930
I can write a good script with him.

15:37.930 --> 15:39.080
And like I always say,

15:40.430 --> 15:43.740
strike while the iron's hot.

15:44.090 --> 15:46.450
That's so dumb. Cut it out.

15:46.450 --> 15:49.930
Got it. And what about the other brat?

15:49.930 --> 15:52.300
Continue to be vigilant.

15:52.300 --> 15:54.290
I'll send Kirara for
extra security later.

15:54.290 --> 15:55.340
Huh?

15:55.340 --> 15:57.540
I'm feeling a nice buzz now.

15:57.540 --> 16:03.430
I haven't felt this alive since
my ex maxed out my credit cards.

16:03.430 --> 16:05.780
Quit bringing up your ex.

16:04.980 --> 16:06.940
Jujutsu High Third-Year, Kinji Hakari

16:04.980 --> 16:06.940
Jujutsu High Third-Year,  Kirara Hoshi

16:08.680 --> 16:10.180
I see.

16:10.180 --> 16:13.130
It sounds like Itadori's going
to be able to contact Hakari.

16:13.520 --> 16:17.540
Why haven't you been able to
see him yet, Panda-senpai?

16:17.540 --> 16:20.330
Well, I do know where he is.

16:20.330 --> 16:22.640
In the monitor room on the roof.

16:22.640 --> 16:25.100
But I can't get close.

16:25.550 --> 16:26.970
You can't get close?

16:26.970 --> 16:30.290
Even when I approach the door,
I can't close the distance.

16:30.290 --> 16:33.750
The sensation feels similar
to Satoru's technique.

16:33.750 --> 16:36.750
It's probably due to Kirara's technique.

16:36.750 --> 16:38.190
Kirara?

16:38.190 --> 16:40.870
But the other third-year was a guy, right?

16:40.870 --> 16:42.250
Yeah.

16:42.250 --> 16:46.600
So does that phenomenon only occur
when Kirara-san's in the monitor room?

16:46.600 --> 16:48.050
I don't know.

16:48.050 --> 16:52.830
I focused on being a circus panda instead
of pushing too far and making them run off.

16:52.830 --> 16:55.160
I'm glad you two showed up.

16:55.610 --> 16:58.200
Do you think Itadori will
succeed in persuading him?

16:58.200 --> 17:02.390
It'll be tough,
but I think it's just a matter of time.

17:02.390 --> 17:06.820
Itadori's bright, charming personality
is a good match for Hakari.

17:06.820 --> 17:08.950
But he sucks at lying, doesn't he?

17:08.950 --> 17:10.770
He doesn't just suck at it.

17:10.770 --> 17:13.330
He struggles to even see
lying as an option.

17:13.330 --> 17:17.540
So once Itadori enters
the monitor room,

17:17.540 --> 17:20.070
I'll take control of the
place quickly and quietly

17:20.070 --> 17:23.040
so I can buy time for the
two of them to talk.

17:23.040 --> 17:24.140
No, that's not...

17:24.140 --> 17:25.070
It'll be fine.

17:25.070 --> 17:26.630
I'll just put them to sleep.

17:26.630 --> 17:29.270
I know where the cameras
and their blind spots are.

17:29.670 --> 17:31.100
How many guards are there?

17:31.360 --> 17:32.710
Four at the entrance,

17:32.710 --> 17:35.190
and two on each floor except the roof.

17:37.740 --> 17:39.160
We can handle that.

17:39.400 --> 17:42.540
The only real concern is
Kirara-san's technique.

17:42.540 --> 17:44.580
We can't do anything about that now.

17:44.580 --> 17:48.510
If they can warp Itadori out
of there or warp in backup,

17:48.510 --> 17:51.090
we'll give up on persuading Hakari.

17:51.090 --> 17:53.560
You're still a first-year, Yu-chan?

17:53.560 --> 17:54.870
You're young.

17:54.870 --> 17:55.620
"Yu-chan"?

17:56.050 --> 17:58.370
Kin-chan had to repeat
a year in middle school.

17:58.780 --> 18:01.070
You sound happy.

18:01.680 --> 18:02.710
Well, yeah.

18:03.170 --> 18:06.260
It's been a while since
Kin-chan's gotten heated up.

18:07.190 --> 18:11.270
You see, I love it when
Kin-chan is passionate.

18:16.340 --> 18:17.480
Itadori.

18:18.000 --> 18:19.920
Would you believe me if I said

18:19.920 --> 18:24.660
you can earn a million yen a month by
doing something for just one hour a day?

18:24.960 --> 18:26.020
Huh?

18:26.020 --> 18:26.780
Hmm?

18:27.230 --> 18:29.900
Depends on what that "something" is.

18:29.900 --> 18:32.120
But you'll have to pay me 200,000 yen

18:32.120 --> 18:34.930
to buy the information on
what that "something" is.

18:34.930 --> 18:36.000
Huh?

18:36.650 --> 18:38.250
I don't believe you, then.

18:38.250 --> 18:43.090
Good. Like you suspected,
that's a classic con.

18:43.090 --> 18:47.300
The swindler pretends to be rich
and sells the means to becoming rich

18:47.300 --> 18:49.060
to scam money from others.

18:49.060 --> 18:51.390
It's obvious if you
think about it logically,

18:51.390 --> 18:54.230
but there's a stupid amount
of fools who fall for it.

18:54.230 --> 18:55.600
Why?

18:55.600 --> 18:58.000
It's all because of passion.

18:58.000 --> 18:59.120
Passion?

18:59.120 --> 19:03.660
Both the swindler and the deceived
have the same passionate drive

19:03.660 --> 19:05.900
to change their lives.

19:06.770 --> 19:10.020
People high on passion lose
sight of their judgment.

19:10.020 --> 19:13.540
Yet no one can fall in love
without passion, either.

19:14.030 --> 19:16.520
I love that passion.

19:17.080 --> 19:21.200
Do you know the most direct way
for people to deal with passion?

19:22.010 --> 19:23.090
Gambling?

19:26.130 --> 19:28.920
I knew you would get it.

19:29.510 --> 19:31.550
Life is a gamble.

19:32.000 --> 19:35.660
Loads of women have dumped me
because they hate gambling,

19:35.660 --> 19:38.080
but they've got it wrong.

19:38.780 --> 19:41.710
Our society throws out
those who can't bet big

19:41.710 --> 19:45.020
and those who don't know when to fold.

19:45.320 --> 19:48.570
There isn't a single person
who doesn't gamble.

19:48.570 --> 19:51.730
What people hate isn't the gambling,

19:51.730 --> 19:54.040
it's losing and being ruined.

19:54.400 --> 19:57.420
Aren't there people who just want
to live a peaceful life, too?

19:57.420 --> 19:59.850
I don't know anyone like that.

20:00.580 --> 20:03.180
I love passion.

20:03.590 --> 20:07.580
Passion is gambling,
and gambling is life.

20:07.580 --> 20:10.000
And love is control.

20:10.510 --> 20:15.150
In the future, I want to control this
nation's passion through my fight club.

20:15.650 --> 20:19.650
With the existence of curses going public
and headquarters barely able to function,

20:19.650 --> 20:22.240
this is my chance to expand the business.

20:22.760 --> 20:24.990
I'm going to crush the
obstacles before me

20:24.990 --> 20:28.620
and make them publicly recognize
my fight club in the coming revisions

20:28.620 --> 20:30.370
to the jujutsu regulations.

20:31.010 --> 20:35.140
At any rate, I'll need a
strong piece on the board.

20:36.280 --> 20:37.620
Itadori...

20:38.490 --> 20:41.650
Want to get high on my passion?

20:42.740 --> 20:45.060
Boss, I need to—

20:57.620 --> 21:00.050
Itadori, want something to drink?

21:00.050 --> 21:02.060
Oh, I'm good with anything.

21:02.060 --> 21:03.420
Other than liquor.

21:03.420 --> 21:05.460
What, can't handle it?

21:05.800 --> 21:08.120
That's not the issue. I'm still underage.

21:08.120 --> 21:10.620
You don't strike me as the
type to care about that.

21:10.620 --> 21:13.760
Did you know Satoru Gojo
can't hold his liquor, either?

21:13.760 --> 21:16.270
Really? Who's Gojo?

21:16.270 --> 21:18.980
And I never said I couldn't.

21:18.980 --> 21:20.310
Look.

21:20.310 --> 21:21.060
Huh?

21:28.780 --> 21:32.450
There isn't a single sorcerer who
doesn't know of Satoru Gojo.

21:32.450 --> 21:34.270
So why did you feign ignorance?

21:34.270 --> 21:35.510
Were you...

21:42.050 --> 21:43.800
sent by Jujutsu High?

21:50.930 --> 21:52.380
Listen! I—

21:52.850 --> 21:54.260
H-Hey!

21:54.260 --> 21:55.650
L-Lis—

21:55.650 --> 21:58.400
When I get a call from Kirara's number,

21:58.400 --> 22:00.850
it's a signal something's up.

22:03.100 --> 22:04.130
Listen to me!

22:04.130 --> 22:05.290
Hell no!

22:05.290 --> 22:06.970
My passion's gone cold now!

22:06.970 --> 22:09.970
Episode 52
Passion

23:40.420 --> 23:42.230
If we can convince them,

23:42.230 --> 23:44.390
negotiations with Hakari-san
will go more smoothly!

23:43.740 --> 23:45.260
Wait, Kirara!

23:45.260 --> 23:46.240
Stay out of this!

23:46.240 --> 23:49.090
You have to show me!
Right here and now!

23:49.090 --> 23:51.020
Please! There's no time!

23:51.020 --> 23:53.460
Kin-chan's in danger!

23:51.990 --> 23:55.060
Next Episode
Cog
